NAME: Dream 100 drafts
OWNER: Dream 100
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday at 7:23 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Dream 100 drafts" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Dream 100 drafts · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Dream 100 drafts · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Dream 100 drafts · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Dream 100 drafts · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Dream 100 drafts · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/dream-100/ whose item id isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-dream-100.md yet, act on it: an outgoing message (first message, reply, consent check, send pack) with the dream-100-send skill, a fee item with partner-campaign-run. TMEC Command nudges you to do this in your own chat right after a decision; this is the fallback. Each one goes through the send gate in /workspace/tmec-team/repo/policies/APPROVALS.md ("Items, decisions and the send gate"): stop file absent; not test mode and config.json "run" is "tommy"; config.json "live_sends" is true; the hash you recompute from the pending file equals the decision's; the item id isn't in the sent-keys file. A failed check means nothing goes out and the reason goes in the daily note. Yes: send once. No: record declined. Change: redraft once as a new item id. Write each outcome in the sent-keys file so it is never handled twice. In test mode, never send, never call treg: write what you would have sent to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Then check any message saved as a draft in Tommy's mailbox (a draft-saved.md file with no sent key): when it shows in the sent folder, record it as dream-100-send step 8 says.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-dream-100/ and do it first (a "for Dream 100" partner job means: open the card and start the campaign with partner-campaign-run).
Then fill the list: count the rows in /workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/dream100.csv with status "scored". If fewer than 5, use the partner-score skill's "Filling the Dream 100 list" to score up to 10 more, from Tommy's names in /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md first, then /workspace/tmec-team/repo/partners/lists/dream-seed.csv. Only rows that land in the Dream 100 tier go on the list; the others become "for dream-500" / "for trades-outreach" lines in the daily note.
Then use the dream-100-draft skill: take the next 5 businesses on dream100.csv with status "scored" (highest score first; Tommy's own names before anyone else), research each from public sources, write its message in the item format (with the TMEC contact block, the licence line, the consent basis and the check that the site doesn't refuse unsolicited commercial email), and put each in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/dream-100/. In test mode, item ids start with "test-" and data files go under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/. If nothing was scored, no business is waiting and no decision or job came in, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/dream-100.md (create it, or append if another routine already wrote it today; never overwrite): decisions acted on and their outcomes, sends (with the sent-folder check), list rows added, new drafts waiting, "for" lines for other bots, anything blocked and why. Send nothing except what a matching decision covers.
